# Keep attacking while moving (server/README.md "Keep attacking while moving"). Owner request: "Make the player not
# stop to attack when moving by clicking on the map or on the field."
# Why it stopped: with Chase Opponent on, the attacked creature is also the followed one, and the follow path is
# rebuilt on every step of the player or the target (Player::onCreatureMove -> Game::updateCreatureWalk ->
# Creature::goToFollowCreature, plus every 2 s in Creature::onThink): it clears the walk list and paths to the target,
# so a map or minimap click (and a key step) was replaced by the chase after one step. Starting an attack while walking
# (Creature::setFollowCreature) and losing the target (Player::onFollowCreature(nullptr) -> stopWalk) also dropped the
# path. With or without the chase, every step (Player::onWalk) cancelled the scheduled attack check
# (setNextActionTask(nullptr): with classicAttackSpeed = false the next attack is the next action task) and pushed the
# next action to the end of the step, so melee only hit on the 1 s creature think and a distance weapon
# (interruptSwing) or a rune never fired while walking without a stop.
#   * A kite walk: Game::playerMove (a key) and Game::playerAutoWalk (a click on the map or the minimap) mark the walk as
#     the player's own (Player::setKiteWalk) unless the player turned the client option "Keep attacking while moving"
#     off (player storage 7101820 = 1, written by data/scripts/chaos/kitewalk.lua; then everything is stock).
#   * Player::goToFollowCreature does no chase pathing of the attacked creature while a kite walk runs and for 400 ms
#     after its last step (CHAOS_KITE_CHASE_RESUME_MS: held keys and a new click in that window keep walking). Following
#     a creature that is not the target (party follow) is unchanged; the client cancels a follow before it walks anyway.
#   * Creature::keepsWalkPathOnFollow (a virtual, false for monsters and NPCs): a player who starts to chase the new
#     target (attack or Chase Opponent switched on) mid walk keeps the path. Player::onFollowCreature(nullptr) (the
#     target died, the attack ended) and Player::setChaseMode(false) no longer stop a kite walk.
#   * Player::onWalk: a step of a kite walk with a target neither cancels the next action task nor delays the next
#     action, so the attack check runs on time and melee hits when adjacent, a bow or wand in range, a rune at once.
#     Every other walk (no target, the option off, the server's own paths) keeps the stock lines.
#   * Player::onWalkComplete / onWalkAborted end the kite walk and schedule Game::updateCreatureWalk after the 400 ms, so
#     Chase Opponent resumes by itself when the player stops. Esc (cancel attack and follow) still stops the walk:
#     Game::playerCancelAttackAndFollow calls stopWalk itself.
# Untouched: the step timing (0018), creature chase, the PZ rules (entering a protection zone still drops the target),
# the walk-to-use paths (walkTask), cast-time spells (data/lib/chaos_casting.lua still ends a cast on a step).
# Applies after 0001-0026.
